-- title:
--   Toric pⁿ-classes specialise to zero
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ such that $p$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data over $A$ in the sense of `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData`, consisting of a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` with `barPt A` followed by $\sigma_A$ equal to `genPt p`, a scheme with relative group law over `base p`, a bijection between $J_H(M/p)$ at the induced level and the sections over `genPt p`, and a bijection `ptsSp` from the degree-zero divisor class group of the residue-field function field onto the sections over `resPt A` followed by $\sigma_A$; and let $O$ be a Néron object `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM A hA \Lambda` over it, with structure morphism $O.g$, relative group law, the bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ between $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field of $X_H(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and the sections of $O.g$ over `genPt p`, and the special-fibre identification $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ of a group of divisor classes with the sections of $O.g$ over `resPt A` followed by $\sigma_A$. Let $n > 0$ and let $x \in J_H(M)$ lie in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^n)$, the subgroup generated by the image of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,(p^n)$. Suppose $s$ is a section of $O.g$ over $\sigma_A$ (a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to O.G$ composing with $O.g$ to $\sigma_A$) such that the morphism attached to $x$ by $O.\mathrm{pts}$ equals `barPt A` followed by $s$, and $s_\kappa$ is a section of $O.g$ over `resPt A` followed by $\sigma_A$ whose underlying morphism is `resPt A` followed by $s$. Then $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}(s_\kappa) = 0$.
--
--   This is the toric clause in the analysis of the special fibre of the Néron model at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level: classes in the toric part of $p^n$-torsion have trivial specialisation, reflecting the vanishing of $\mu_{p^n}$ over an algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$. It is used by the statement on $p^n$-torsion classes and their images in the abelian quotient, [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_mem_finPts_toPic0Pair_ptsSp_symm_eq_and_eq_zero_iff_and_of_mem_toricPts_of_not_sq_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_mem_finPts_toPic0Pair_ptsSp_symm_eq_and_eq_zero_iff_and_of_mem_toricPts_of_not_sq_dvd).
